    "id": "p52-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Show that $y=5x-7$ is perpendicular to $5y=10-x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$5\\times\\left(-\\frac15\\right)=-1$, so the lines are perpendicular.",
      "worked": "Line 1: $y=5x-7$, so $m_1=5$.\n\nLine 2:\n$$\\begin{aligned}5y&=10-x\\\\y&=2-\\frac{x}{5}\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $m_2=-\\frac15$.\n$$m_1m_2=5\\times\\left(-\\frac15\\right)=-1$$\nThe lines are perpendicular.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
